			"Message": "docs(Sky): Refine terminology for bundled workbench pipeline\n\nClarify the description of the bundling process in the README by replacing the phrase \"pipeline that pre-compiles\" with \"compilation pipeline that pre-compiles into...\" for grammatical precision. Also change \"core workbench\" to \"core workbench\" (lowercase) to maintain consistent terminology regarding the VS Code integration.\n\nThese minor edits ensure the documentation accurately reflects the technical flow where Vite/Rollup compile variants into specific chunks within the `Target/Static/Bundled/` directory, without altering any functional behavior.",
